WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:03.340
"Dune" is a movie full of loose ends.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:06.859
Onscreen the film is titled "Dune: Part One,"
and it covers a little less than half of the

00:00:06.859 --> 00:00:08.860
story of the book that it's based on.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:10.700
What's left hanging when the credits roll?

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.809
These are the biggest unanswered questions
in Dune.

00:00:13.809 --> 00:00:17.439
Around the film's extravagant midway point,
when the Harkonnens have laid slaughter to

00:00:17.439 --> 00:00:21.349
House Atreides with a dual pronged attack
and help from the Emperor's warrior force

00:00:21.349 --> 00:00:25.320
the Sardaukar, the final fate of several characters
remains left open.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:29.000
Duncan Idaho, Paul's trainer and friend, survives
the battle and makes it out alive to help

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.910
Paul and Lady Jessica make it to safety.

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:34.210
But what about the rest of House Atreides'
high-ranking men?

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:38.590
There are two prominent figures we never see
in the aftermath of all that carnage: Gurney

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:44.540
Halleck, the weapons master, and Thufir Hawat,
the Mentat, or advisor, to Duke Leto Atreides.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:48.460
Those familiar with the source material know
both men survive, but with differing paths

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:50.470
from this particular catastrophe.

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:55.290
Gurney survives the battle and becomes a smuggler,
disillusioned by what has transpired and mistakenly

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:59.170
thinking Lady Jessica was in some way responsible
for Duke Leto's death.

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:03.510
But Thufir is kept on by the Harkonnens to
replace the recently deceased Piter De Vries

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:08.070
as their new Mentat, a position he uses to
undermine their regime from within.

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:11.780
But that's assuming that the filmmakers behind
the new "Dune" movie plan to keep things as

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:14.990
close to the novel as possible in a potential
sequel.

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:17.750
"There's a crusade coming."

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:23.280
In "Dune: Part One," Dr. Liet-Kynes is portrayed
by actress Sharon Duncan-Brewster in one of

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:24.870
the film's more affecting performances.

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:29.100
Though the character is canonically male in
the source material, this iteration is not

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.260
drastically different in practice.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:35.330
Introduced as an objective observer of the
regime change between the Harkonnens and House

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:39.560
Atreides, it becomes clear that while Dr.
Kynes is loyal to neither opposing force,

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:44.010
she is also not exactly loyal to the Emperor,
instead considering herself a Fremen first

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:45.150
and foremost.

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:50.080
"Dune" 2021 portrays Dr. Kynes as an impartial
emissary of the emperor whose heart belongs

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:54.479
with the native people of Arrakis, who worships
Shai-Hulud, and who has a murky, unexplored

00:01:54.479 --> 00:01:56.800
past with a Fremen lover who died.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:01.200
But one key element missing from this film
is that Dr. Kynes has a child, Chani, a Fremen

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.780
played by Zendaya.

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:06.790
Chani doesn't appear onscreen until the film's
final act, only showing up throughout in Paul's

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:08.140
visions of the future.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:12.530
Dr. Kynes seemingly meets her fate by being
swallowed up by the great sandworm before

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:16.209
the film's last act, so we never see any interaction
between the two characters.

00:02:16.209 --> 00:02:20.459
It remains to be seen if a "Part Two" will
follow up with this information, or perhaps

00:02:20.459 --> 00:02:25.299
even delve into Dr. Kynes' origins as a half-Fremen
as outlined in Brian Herbert and Kevin J.

00:02:25.299 --> 00:02:27.299
Anderson's "Prelude to Dune."

00:02:27.299 --> 00:02:29.519
In this movie, maybe they're related, and
maybe they're not.

00:02:30.519 --> 00:02:38.099
"How can the emperor take everything we've
built and give it to that filth?"

00:02:38.099 --> 00:02:42.220
One side effect of cutting the book's plot
in half: One of the key figures in the "Dune"

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:46.340
mythology, the character who sets everything
into motion, is completely absent from "Dune:

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:47.340
Part One."

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:52.480
The Padishah Emperor, Shaddam IV, previously
played onscreen by Jose Ferrer in David Lynch's

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:57.169
1984 version, is nowhere to be found, only
alluded to as the catalyst for replacing the

00:02:57.169 --> 00:02:59.689
Harkonnens on Arrakis with House Atreides.

00:02:59.689 --> 00:03:04.219
Likewise, his daughter, Princess Irulan, also
a key figure in the plot, has yet to be seen

00:03:04.219 --> 00:03:05.219
either.

00:03:05.219 --> 00:03:08.999
It makes sense to not bother casting actors
for parts that won't have much dialogue until

00:03:08.999 --> 00:03:10.389
a potential sequel.

00:03:10.389 --> 00:03:14.549
But in sidelining the Emperor, the motivations
for his plot against Duke Leto are left harder

00:03:14.549 --> 00:03:16.590
to parse than they would otherwise be.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:20.099
Moviegoers will just have to wait for part
two to find out exactly what the Emperor is

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:21.120
thinking with all of this.

00:03:22.269 --> 00:03:26.010
In one of the film's most touching sequences,
not long before House Atreides suffers such

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:30.739
heavy casualties, Duke Leto can feel the walls
closing around him and he makes a heartbreaking

00:03:30.739 --> 00:03:32.709
confession to Lady Jessica.

00:03:32.709 --> 00:03:36.239
While she consoles him over the growing fears
this move to Arrakis has been little more

00:03:36.239 --> 00:03:39.900
than a trap, he tells her how much he regrets
not marrying her.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:44.530
Lady Jessica was a concubine, and a sister
of the Bene Gesserit, so her siring a son

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.499
with Leto was unconventional.

00:03:46.499 --> 00:03:49.579
But he allowed her to raise their son and
teach him the Weirding Way.

00:03:49.579 --> 00:03:53.779
Knowing that in all likelihood, he's not long
for this world, he asks her and the Bene Gesserit

00:03:53.779 --> 00:03:54.909
to protect his son.

00:03:54.909 --> 00:03:58.820
While it isn't as essential to the plot as
some of the other unanswered questions, Leto

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:02.219
and Jessica leave the viewer wanting more
of their history together, to know what kept

00:04:02.219 --> 00:04:04.609
Duke Leto from making an honest woman out
of Lady Jessica.

00:04:05.609 --> 00:04:09.239
It's going to be pretty disappointing if this
adaptation doesn't continue with a big-screen

00:04:09.239 --> 00:04:10.669
"Dune: Part Two."

00:04:10.669 --> 00:04:14.540
When this first movie was greenlit, that was
far from a guarantee, but the people behind

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:18.790
the movie seem confident in the likelihood
of a sequel that finishes the story.

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:20.890
And that's just regarding the first book.

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:24.820
Frank Herbert's original source material takes
this saga even further into the future with

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:28.600
several sequels, including the books "Dune
Messiah" and "Children of Dune."

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:32.730
Director Denis Villeneuve is on record as
saying his plan isn't just an adaptation of

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:36.810
the original book split in two, but rather
a trilogy of films that would culminate in

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:41.150
a third chapter with "Dune Messiah" serving
as its own standalone film to conclude Paul

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:42.450
Atreides' story.

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:46.040
We also still have "Dune: The Sisterhood,"
a prequel series about the origins of the

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:48.820
Bene Gesserit, being developed and waiting
in the wings.

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:52.000
A lot is riding on this film's financial success.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.390
Above all else, the spice must flow.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:56.790
"This is only the beginning."

